    {
        "id": "8d24f276d123a072",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Kafka 07: error handling",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Catch messages that could not be sent, and raise an alert when a Kafka node loses or regains its connection.",
        "env": []
    },
    {
        "id": "6620e24d9a80daee",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "8d24f276d123a072",
        "name": "Example 07: error handling with catch and status nodes - select me and open the Info sidebar",
        "info": "## Error handling with *catch* and *status*\n\nThe Kafka nodes never crash Node-RED. Problems are reported in three places:\n\n1. **The node status** (and *status* nodes): the connection state, e.g. `connected` (green), `ECONNREFUSED localhost:9092 · retry 8s` (yellow, Kafka unreachable, retrying), `auth failed · retry 60s` (red, needs a human).\n2. **Catch nodes**: a message that could not be handled ends with an error; a *catch* node receives the original message with `msg.error`.\n3. **The Node-RED log**: the first failure of an outage is logged as an error, then only a warning every 10th attempt, so the log does not fill up.\n\n**Before you deploy:** the example connects to a Kafka broker on `localhost:9092`. If yours runs elsewhere, double-click any Kafka node, click the pencil next to **Broker** (the configuration node *Local Kafka (example 07)*) and change **Brokers**. Then click **Deploy**.\n\n**Topics:** the producer creates `example-errors` with its first message if the broker allows automatic topic creation (Apache Kafka does by default, many managed services do not). Until a topic exists, the consumer shows `unknown topic/partition · retry …` (yellow) and keeps retrying, waiting a little longer each time; it starts at the first retry after the topic was created. To create topics yourself, use the admin node (example 06) or your Kafka tools.\n\n### Try it\n\n- Click **valid message**: it is sent (delivery report).\n- Click **topic sensors/temp**: Kafka topic names may only contain letters, digits, `.`, `_` and `-`, so the producer rejects the message and the catch node gets it.\n- Click **no topic**: neither the node nor `msg.topic` names a topic.\n- Stop Kafka. After a short while (kafkajs retries first) the consumer status turns yellow and the *connecting / retrying* debug node shows it once. The producer only notices when it sends: click **valid message**. Its offline queue is **Off**, so the message fails and goes to the catch node. Start Kafka again: the statuses turn green and *connected again* shows it. (Instead of stopping Kafka you can also set the broker address to a port nothing listens on and deploy.)\n\nReplace the debug nodes by an e-mail, Telegram, MQTT or dashboard node to get real alerts.",
        "x": 400,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
