    {
        "id": "0f8d9b330ad89f92",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "8d24f276d123a072",
        "name": "Alert when the connection state changes",
        "info": "The *status* node receives every status change of the producer and the consumer: `msg.status = { fill, shape, text, source: { id, type, name } }`. The *filter* node (rbe) only lets a message through when the colour of a node changes, so a retry countdown does not raise a new alert every time. The *switch* routes by colour:\n\n- **red**: a problem that does not fix itself (wrong password, not authorised, TLS or configuration error). The node keeps retrying slowly.\n- **yellow**: connecting, or Kafka unreachable and the node is retrying (messages are queued if the producer has an offline queue).\n- **green**: connected again.",
        "x": 230,
        "y": 340,
        "wires": []
    },
